$DIR/main.p:17:14: cannot store makeBig() in i, which outlives the temporary
    The Big that makeBig() returns (at main.p:17) is a temporary: nothing keeps
    it, so it is the receiver of the method only until the end of the statement.
    A view of it may be passed to calls in that statement but may not outlive
    it. At the end of the statement, the temporary is dropped, but i lives
    longer, so it would be left pointing at a value that has been dropped.
    The view does not own the memory it looks at. Nothing keeps the temporary
    after the statement, so a stored view would outlive the value that keeps its
    memory alive.
    Keep the owner in a variable, so that it lives until the end of its scope,
    and take the view through that variable:
        v := makeBig()
        ... v ...
    (see "Views" in the Plutonium spec, section 18.3)
    (run "pluto explain E3009" for a longer explanation)

